03. PROJECT DESIGN

Project Title

LegalEaseAI – AI-Powered Legal Document Generator

1. Introduction

The project design phase explains how the LegalEaseAI system will be structured and how its different components will communicate with each other.

2. System Architecture

The system consists of the following major components:

1. User Interface
2. FastAPI Backend
3. Input Processing Module
4. Generative AI Model
5. Document Generation Module
6. Output Interface

3. System Flow

User
↓
Web Interface
↓
FastAPI Backend
↓
User Input Processing
↓
Generative AI Model
↓
Document Generation
↓
Generated Document
↓
User Review / Download

4. User Interface Design

The application can contain the following pages:

Home Page

Provides information about LegalEaseAI and allows the user to start generating a document.

Input Page

Allows the user to select the document type and enter the required information.

Result Page

Displays the document generated by the AI model.

5. Backend Design

FastAPI is used as the backend framework.

The backend handles:

1. User requests
2. Application routing
3. Input processing
4. Communication with the AI model
5. Generation of the response
6. Returning the result to the user

6. AI Module

The AI module receives the user's requirements and generates a structured legal document based on the selected document type and provided information.

7. Workflow

1. User opens the application.
2. User selects a document type.
3. User enters required information.
4. The request is sent to FastAPI.
5. FastAPI processes the input.
6. The input is sent to the Generative AI model.
7. The AI model generates the document.
8. The generated document is returned to the application.
9. The user reviews the document.
10. The user can save or download the result.

8. Conclusion

The project design provides a clear structure for implementing LegalEaseAI. It defines the user interface, backend, AI integration, workflow, and output process.